---
description: Protect test and evaluation integrity
globs: tests/**,evals/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Never delete, skip, loosen or rewrite an assertion to make a test pass.
- If a test fails, report the failure and fix the code, or ask the owner.
- Evals assert on database state and mock-provider records, not only response text.
- Keep a held-out eval subset; do not tune prompts against it.
- Do not invent or hardcode result numbers; report what the run produced.
- Integration tests roll back their transaction and must not leave data behind.
